# Vercel CLI deploys upload the whole repo (site/'s sibling `file:` packages need to be present on
# disk at build time — see site/README.md). .vercelignore, not .gitignore, controls what's excluded
# here, because .gitignore excludes contracts/out/ (a build artifact we don't want in git) but the
# deployed site needs that exact artifact present (lib/artifact.ts reads it) and there's no Foundry
# toolchain on Vercel's build image to regenerate it. If this file didn't exist, Vercel CLI would fall
# back to .gitignore and silently ship a broken build.
node_modules
.git
.next
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
.env.local
.DS_Store
contracts/lib
contracts/cache
contracts/broadcast
